;; Phase 0 — no-op sandbox.
;;
;; Purpose: prove that wrapping `claude --remote-control` in sandbox-exec at all
;; doesn't break dyld, subprocess spawning, or the Fleet pairing handshake,
;; BEFORE any real restriction enters the picture.
;;
;; The two file-write denials below are NOT part of the diagnostic. They are a
;; deliberate data-safety guard: this run also carries
;; --dangerously-skip-permissions, so there is no app-layer boundary either.
;; Denying writes to the Obsidian vault and the Bear database cannot affect the
;; Phase 0 exit criteria (dyld / fork / network handshake), so it costs nothing
;; diagnostically. If Phase 0 fails, re-test with these two lines removed to
;; rule them out before concluding anything.

(version 1)

(allow default)

(deny file-write*
  (subpath "/Users/brianlow/Library/Mobile Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Brian's Vault")
  (subpath "/Users/brianlow/Library/Group Containers/9K33E3U3T4.net.shinyfrog.bear"))
